{"archetypes":[{"name":"shell-failure","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes Bash failure handling under set -euo pipefail where small control-flow mistakes can bypass structured outcomes.","prompt_body":"Investigate the Bash control flow in scripts/design-pause-load.sh and scripts/design-log-publish.sh for failure paths that could bypass structured KV output or exit unexpectedly under set -euo pipefail. Pay particular attention to guarded git ls-tree/show calls, temp NUL-buffer handling, marker-delete warning behavior, and allowlist validation branches. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"git-snapshot","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The restore primitive changes from git archive to ls-tree/show and needs specialist scrutiny across refs, attributes, and path safety.","prompt_body":"Review the snapshot restoration design in scripts/design-pause-load.sh for interactions with git refs, export-ignore attributes, subtree enumeration, and blob extraction. Check whether the implementation safely handles empty snapshots, weird filenames, ref selection, path prefix validation, and partial extraction failures without installing inconsistent state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"resume-state","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The patch changes pause marker lifecycle semantics, which can create stale-marker or lost-resume regressions across workflow boundaries.","prompt_body":"Examine the pause/resume state machine across loader behavior, publisher behavior, docs, and tests. Focus on whether marker keep-on-failure and delete-on-success semantics are implemented consistently, whether WARN=marker-delete-failed preserves operator recovery options, and whether documented contracts match actual lifecycle transitions. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
